---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **어느 두 별자리가 한 그룹에 같이 있나.** (`/star-sign-pairs`)
 *
 * 🔴 [2026-09-06] 사장님이 점성학 검색어를 세 층으로 갈라 주셨다. 맨 아래 «구매 의도» 층의
 *   첫 낱말이 **Compatibility** 였다. 우리 별자리 지면 열두 장을 열어 보니 그 낱말이 **0번**.
 *
 * ⛔ 그런데 우리는 궁합을 봐 줄 수 없다. 그것은 점이다.
 * ⭐ 대신 아무도 안 센 것을 낸다 — 「실제 케이팝 그룹에서 이 두 별자리가 몇 번 한 팀이었나.」
 *   그리고 «기대값»을 나란히 놓는다. 실측만 내면 사람이 뜻을 지어낸다.
 *
 * ⭐⭐ 답이 「아무것도 안 갈린다」로 나왔다. 그것이 이 지면의 값어치다 —
 *   궁합을 파는 곳은 절대 이 표를 안 낸다. 우리는 낸다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 안 하는 것 ─────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ 「이 둘은 잘 맞는다」를 한 줄도 안 쓴다.
 * ⛔ 배수가 1.25 인 짝을 「많다」고 부르지 않는다 — 표준편차 안이다.
 * ⛔ z 값을 확정처럼 내지 않는다. 한 사람이 여러 짝에 들어가 짝끼리 독립이 아니다.
 *
 * 🔴 Astro 앞말은 TypeScript 다. 🔴 JSX 는 끝 공백을 버린다 — {' '} 를 쓴다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import KcwMethodLimits from '../../components/KcwMethodLimits.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-sign-pairs.json';

type 줄 = {
  pair: string; a: string; b: string; same: boolean;
  observed: number; expected: number | null; ratio: number | null; groups: string[];
};

const 큰글자 = (s: string) => s.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + s.slice(1);
const 짝글 = (r: 줄) => `${큰글자(r.a)} + ${큰글자(r.b)}`;

const 줄들 = (d.rows as any[]) as 줄[];
const 많은순 = [...줄들].sort((x, y) => y.observed - x.observed);
const 으뜸 = 많은순[0];
/* 배수는 «기대값이 넉넉한 짝»에서만 견준다 — 기대 5짜리 짝의 배수는 잡음이다 */
const 견줄만한것 = 줄들.filter((r) => (r.expected ?? 0) >= 20 && r.ratio !== null);
const 배수순 = [...견줄만한것].sort((x, y) => (y.ratio ?? 0) - (x.ratio ?? 0));
const 가장높은배수 = 배수순[0];
const 가장낮은배수 = 배수순[배수순.length - 1];

/* 🔴 제목·본문이 말하는 수가 자료와 어긋나면 빌드를 세운다 */
if (!으뜸 || !가장높은배수 || !가장낮은배수) throw new Error('짝 줄이 모자라다 — 이 지면은 표에서 시작한다.');
if (줄들.length !== 78) throw new Error(`짝이 ${줄들.length}개다 — 별자리 열둘이면 78이어야 한다.`);
if ((가장높은배수.ratio ?? 0) >= 1.5 || (가장낮은배수.ratio ?? 9) <= 0.5) {
  throw new Error(`배수가 ${가장낮은배수.ratio}~${가장높은배수.ratio} 다 — 「아무것도 안 갈린다」가 더는 맞지 않는다. 본문을 다시 쓴다.`);
}

const 쉼표 = (n: number | null) => (n === null ? '—' : Number(n).toLocaleString('en-US'));

const TITLE = 'Which star signs actually end up in the same K-pop group';
const DESC =
  `We counted all ${쉼표(d.totalPairs)} pairings of members inside ${d.groupsCounted} K-pop groups and set each `
  + `pair of star signs beside what chance alone would give. Every pair lands between `
  + `${가장낮은배수.ratio}x and ${가장높은배수.ratio}x. Nothing sorts.`;

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  variableMeasured: ['Observed co-membership count per star-sign pair', 'Expected count under chance'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/star-sign-pairs">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    If you came looking for zodiac compatibility, this is what we can honestly show you: not whether two
    signs get along, but how often they have actually stood on the same stage.
  </p>

  <p class="q">
    <b>We do not read star signs.</b> Every number here is a count of recorded birth dates. There is no
    claim anywhere on this page that one pairing is better than another.
  </p>

  <h2>The answer first</h2>

  <p>
    Across <b>{d.groupsCounted} K-pop groups</b> and <b>{쉼표(d.peopleCounted)} members</b> whose birth date
    is on record, there are <b>{쉼표(d.totalPairs)} pairings</b> of one member with another. The most common
    pairing of signs is <b>{짝글(으뜸)}</b>, {으뜸.observed} times. Chance alone would give
    {' '}{으뜸.expected}.
  </p>

  <p>
    <b>That is the whole story.</b> Of the 78 possible pairs, the one furthest above chance is
    {' '}{짝글(가장높은배수)} at <b>{가장높은배수.ratio}&times;</b>, and the one furthest below is
    {' '}{짝글(가장낮은배수)} at <b>{가장낮은배수.ratio}&times;</b>. With counts this size, gaps that
    size are what randomness produces. <b>No two signs find each other, and no two avoid each other.</b>
  </p>

  <h2>Every pair, most common first</h2>

  <div class="scroll-x">
    <table>
      {/* 🔴 [2026-09-06] 렌더해서 보니 예시 칸에 큰 그룹이 거의 모든 줄에 나온다. 감추지 않고 적는다 —
          멤버가 많은 팀은 짝을 많이 만들어 내니 당연히 자주 나온다. 그 당연함을 안 적으면
          보는 사람이 「고장 났나」 하거나 「이 팀이 특별한가」로 읽는다. */}
      <caption>
        Times two signs were in the same group, against what chance would give. Measured {d.measuredAt}.
        The large groups appear in nearly every row simply because more members make more pairings.
      </caption>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Pair</th><th>Together</th><th>By chance</th><th>Ratio</th><th>For example</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {많은순.map((r) => (
          <tr class={r.same ? 'same' : undefined}>
            <th scope="row">{짝글(r)}{r.same && <span class="tag">same sign</span>}</th>
            <td class="num">{r.observed}</td>
            <td class="num">{r.expected}</td>
            <td class="num">{r.ratio === null ? '—' : `${r.ratio}×`}</td>
            <td class="eg">{r.groups.slice(0, 3).join(', ') || '—'}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Why a pair is common has nothing to do with the pair</h2>

  <p>
    {짝글(으뜸)} tops the table because those are two of the commonest signs among K-pop members, not
    because anything draws them together. That is exactly why the <b>by chance</b> column is here. A raw
    count on its own invites a reader to find meaning in it; the two columns side by side take that back.
  </p>

  <p>
    The one place our data does bend is <b>the calendar, not the pairing</b> &mdash; K-pop birthdays are
    not spread evenly through the year, and July is the thinnest month.
    {' '}<a href="/kpop-birthdays">We measured that separately</a>, and it is a fact about when
    people are born in Korea rather than about star signs.
  </p>

  <h2>What we could not measure</h2>
  <ul>{d.notMeasured.map((s: string) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>

  <h2>Two things that would bend these numbers</h2>
  <ul>{d.caveats.map((s: string) => <li>{s}</li>)}</ul>

  <p class="note">
    One more, and it cuts against us: a member sits in many pairings at once, so the pairs are not
    independent of one another. Any test that treats them as independent will overstate how surprising a
    gap is. We mention it because it makes our own &ldquo;nothing sorts&rdquo; conclusion <em>stronger</em>,
    and a limitation that only ever helps the writer is worth suspecting.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <p class="walk">
    <a href="/star-sign/leo">The twelve signs, one page each</a> &middot;{' '}
    <a href="/star-signs">Does a birth year sign predict charting?</a> &middot;{' '}
    <a href="/bts-star-signs">BTS, seven members and six signs</a> &middot;{' '}
    <a href="/kpop-birthdays">Which month K-pop is born in</a>
  </p>

  <KcwMethodLimits
    method={{
      'What this is': d.whatThisIs,
      'How we counted': `Every group with at least two members whose birth date is recorded. For each group `
        + `we formed every pair of members and tallied their two signs. The expected column spreads signs `
        + `at the rate they occur in this population and assumes each seat is filled independently.`,
      'Who is left out': `${d.peopleWithoutSign} members have no birth date on record. They are left out `
        + `rather than filled in, so every figure here describes the ${쉼표(d.peopleCounted)} we could count.`,
    }}
    limitation={{
      'What this is not': 'Not compatibility, not a reading, and not advice. We count who was in a band '
        + 'with whom. Whether that means anything is not something a birth date can answer.',
    }} />

  <p class="asof">Measured {d.measuredAt}.</p>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/star-sign-pairs" />
</WikiTip>

<style>
  .lead { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .q { background: #f6f7f9; border-left: 3px solid #999; padding: .7rem .9rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: .95rem; }
  caption { text-align: left; font-weight: 600; padding-bottom: .4rem; }
  th, td { border-bottom: 1px solid #e3e5e8; padding: .4rem .6rem; text-align: left; }
  th { background: #fafbfc; }
  td.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  td.eg { color: #555; font-size: .9rem; }
  tr.same th { background: #f3f0fa; }
  .tag { display: inline-block; margin-left: .4rem; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 400;
         color: #6b5aa0; border: 1px solid #d7cfe9; border-radius: 3px; padding: 0 .3rem; }
  .note { font-size: .95rem; color: #555; background: #fbfbfc; border-left: 3px solid #ddd;
          padding: .6rem .9rem; }
  .walk { font-size: .95rem; margin: .6rem 0 1.2rem; }
  .asof { font-size: .85rem; color: #666; margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .scroll-x { overflow-x: auto; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .q { background: #1c1f24; border-left-color: #666; }
    th { background: #1a1d21; }
    th, td { border-bottom-color: #2a2e34; }
    tr.same th { background: #241f31; }
    .tag { color: #b3a4dd; border-color: #453a63; }
    td.eg { color: #aaa; }
    .note { background: #191b1f; border-left-color: #333; color: #aaa; }
    .asof { color: #999; }
  }
</style>
